y putt and I'm  a very bad putter  the last gadget to suffer through  playing a round of golf with me was the  Garmin approach s6 watch which really  does a combination of all the other  gadgets because the watch has GPS and  all the maps of the US course is built  right in it located what whole I was at  and how far I was from it more useful  where the arrows here that tell me what  direction I should hit my ball  there are also swing speed tools in here  but the interface is clumsy and the  touchscreen really doesn't work well you  know if you spent as much time  practicing as you did playing with that  watch and that's what I discovered I  liked the Archos and the Zep the best  because they quietly collected  information and didn't require me to  futz with them it was all about  concentrating on the game I love to play  now can someone just create a track of a  ball maybe something with Bluetooth so  we can find the darn thing
 

